    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as the primary offensive engine for LawDog with an elite efficiency score of 74.61. His favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a, combined with a significant park factor boost and strong platoon leverage, positions him as the cornerstone of our lineup. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (66.12) and **Bryson Stott** (63.92) are high-confidence starts. **Daulton Varsho** benefits from a soft matchup against Rea and positive park dynamics, while **Bryson Stott** capitalizes on the stolen base potential afforded by a slow-working pitcher, neutralizing the perceived difficulty of facing Peralta. We are also leaning on **Geraldo Perdomo** (60.32), whose consistent presence in the #2 hole against Bradley provides a reliable floor for both runs and average.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the margins involved **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Taylor Ward**. **Taylor Ward** was weighed down by a difficult matchup against Yamamoto, though he remains in the lineup due to a favorable wind forecast and high-leverage order placement. **Drew Gilbert** barely held onto his spot with a 40.95 score; his involvement is heavily penalized by his position at the bottom of the order and the presence of a tough opponent in Meyer. Regarding our bench, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Dylan Beavers** remain unavailable due to injury or roster status, leaving our depth options limited. We are closely monitoring the status of **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Gavin Sheets**, but none currently offer a higher efficiency profile than our projected starters given the scarcity of speed in today's matchups. Caution is advised with **Cal Raleigh** and **Matt Chapman**, as both are battling sub-optimal conditions against high-end starting pitching, making them our most volatile assets today.",
